# Story: As a terminal planner, I want each container to have at most one open booking, so that two trucks are never sent for the same container. If a container already has a booking that is BOOKED, another booking for it (by anyone, for any slot) is refused with DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_BOOKING. After the first booking is cancelled the container can be booked again.

@draft
Feature: Container Booking Rules

  Scenario Outline: A container can only have one open booking
    Given a gate slot tomorrow at 10:00 with room for 2 trucks
    And I am a driver
    When I book that slot for a valid container "<container>"
    Then the booking is confirmed with a reference
    And another driver tries to book that slot for the same container "<container>"
    Then their booking is refused because "DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_BOOKING"
    And I cancel my booking
    Then my booking is "CANCELLED"
    And the slot has 2 places left

    Examples:
      | container |
      | C1        |
      | C2        |

  Scenario Outline: Booking a container with an existing active booking fails
    Given another driver books that slot for the same container "<container>"
    When I try to book that slot for the same container "<container>"
    Then the booking is refused because "DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_BOOKING"
    And another driver looks up my booking
    Then they are told it does not exist

  Scenario Outline: Canceling a booking frees up the slot
    Given I have booked that slot for a valid container "<container>"
    When I cancel my booking
    Then my booking is "CANCELLED"
    And the slot has 2 places left

  Scenario: Booking after cancellation works
    Given another driver books that slot for the same container "<container>"
    And I cancel my booking
    When I try to book that slot for the same container "<container>"
    Then the booking is confirmed with a reference
    And the slot has 1 place left

